## Scope and originality

This is an **original implementation** of a serial-port monitoring tool, written to
interoperate with standard serial devices and the public Modbus specification.

* All source code, UI, strings and assets in this repository were created for this
  project. No third-party code, icons or text were copied.
* Protocol behaviour (Modbus RTU / ASCII / TCP) implements the publicly documented
  Modbus protocol, including its published CRC-16/LRC checksums.
* The Windows techniques used (IAT and inline function hooking, device-stack filter
  drivers, IRP completion routines, device namespace enumeration) are documented by
  Microsoft in the Win32 and WDK documentation and are common to any serial tool.

This project is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by any other software
vendor. Any product names that appear in build scripts or documentation do so only to
identify file formats or OS components, and remain the trademarks of their owners.

If you intend to redistribute a **built binary** that includes the kernel driver, you
need your own code-signing certificate. The test certificate used during local
development is deliberately not included in this repository (see `.gitignore` and
`SECURITY.md`).

## Security

See `SECURITY.md` for how to report a vulnerability.
